  "flow_summary": "The system handled the initial intake well but entered an infinite, repetitive loop once the safety protocol was triggered. Despite the patient consistently answering 'I don't know' to questions about the status of emergency responders, the system failed to recognize this as a terminal state for that line of questioning and continued to cycle through the same instructions and inquiries indefinitely.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "repetition",
      "evidence": "The system repeatedly asked the patient to check their phone connection and call 911, despite the patient consistently responding 'I don't know' or 'Yes' to previous prompts, resulting in a loop of over 50 redundant turns."
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "failure_to_accept_unknown",
      "evidence": "The system failed to accept the patient's repeated 'I don't know' responses regarding the status of emergency responders, instead continuing to press for information that the patient clearly could not provide."
    }
